WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A landscape, written in mathematics. Geometry. Materials. Light. Volume. A camera.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
First, give the world a shape. Scaled, displaced sphere meshes establish the inlet.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Let the stone become irregular. Sine, cosine and seeded Perlin fields form the radial relief.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Three waves give the water its shape. The terms add together to displace the water surface.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The surfaces catch their reflections. Procedural bump, roughness and a thin coat create the wet surfaces.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Light turns the construction into a place. Warm grazing light meets cool fill and the sky.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Mist gives the distance its depth. A height-dependent density field scatters and attenuates the light.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
TIDELIGHT Explore the equations. Rebuild the scene.

